provided Ric_g is *defined* via the conformal Ricci formula: Ric_g = −(n−2)λ^{−1}Hess_δ λ − λ^{−1}Δ_δλ δ − (n−2)λ^{−2}|dλ|²δ + 2(n−2)λ^{−2}dλ⊗dλ. Hmm, that's the general conformal Ricci. If I take that as the definition of Ric in the model, the Bochner identity becomes a pure algebraic identity in λ and u, provable by expanding everything — the λ-terms cancel. This is doable but the general-λ computation is gnarly.

