lemma deriv_lapG_eq (hu2 : DifferentiableAt ℝ (deriv u) r)
    (hu3 : DifferentiableAt ℝ (deriv (deriv u)) r) (hm : DifferentiableAt ℝ m r) :
    deriv (lapG n m u) r = deriv (deriv (deriv u)) r + (n : ℝ) * (deriv m r * deriv u r + m r * deriv (deriv u) r) := by
  change deriv (fun s => deriv (deriv u) s + (n : ℝ) * m s * deriv u s) r = _
  have h1 : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fun s => deriv (deriv u) s) r := hu3
  have h2 : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fun s => (n : ℝ) * m s * deriv u s) r := by
    exact (((hm.const_mul (n : ℝ))).mul hu2)  -- (fun s => (n:ℝ) * m s) mul (deriv u)
  rw [deriv_add h1 h2]
  rw [deriv_const_mul (n : ℝ) ((hm.mul hu2))]
  rw [deriv_mul hm hu2]
  ring
```
Careful: (n:ℝ) * m s * deriv u s parses as ((n:ℝ) * m s) * deriv u s. deriv of fun s => (n:ℝ)*m s: deriv_const_mul (n:ℝ) hm : deriv (fun s => (n:ℝ) * m s) r = (n:ℝ) * deriv m r ✓. deriv_mul of (fun s => (n:ℝ)*m s) and (deriv u): hmm the deriv_mul application: deriv_mul (hmul : DifferentiableAt ...) (hu2) : deriv ((fun s => (n:ℝ)*m s) * (deriv u)) r = deriv ((fun s => (n:ℝ)*m s)) r * deriv u r + (fun s => (n:ℝ)*m s) r * deriv (deriv u) r. And fun s => (n:ℝ)*m s * deriv u s is the product of those two functions ✓ (pointwise). OK.

