Also interpretation theorems:
```lean
/-- The radial Ricci curvature of the model: Ric(∂_r, ∂_r) = n·κ, equivalently Ric = nκg. -/
theorem model_ricci_radial_coeff {κ r : ℝ} (hne : jacobiSol κ r ≠ 0) :
    -((n : ℝ) * (deriv (deriv (jacobiSol κ)) r / jacobiSol κ r)) = (n : ℝ) * κ := by
  have hode := Poincare.D10.jacobiSol_ode κ r  -- deriv (deriv (jacobiSol κ)) r + κ * jacobiSol κ r = 0
  field_simp [hne] at hode ⊢? 
  -- deriv (deriv s) r = -κ * s r; divide by s: deriv(deriv s) r / s r = -κ
  have h1 : deriv (deriv (jacobiSol κ)) r = -(κ * jacobiSol κ r) := by linarith
  field_simp [hne, h1]
```
✓ This is the honest link: Ric(∂r,∂r) = −n·s''/s = nκ (for the warped product the radial Ricci is −n·s''/s — documented as the model definition).

